      "body": "Fixes #8007\n\n`TestServerKeysAnotherHostWritesAreRecordedNotRefused` isolated only `HOME`/`XDG_CONFIG_HOME` for its merged-load half, but the config chain is governed by whatever the host supplies — the same isolation shape #7686 fixed in the gen property test:\n\n- an ambient `MCPX_PATHS_CONFIG` seed with no null replaces the discovery walk outright, so the fixture never loads;\n- without a seed, `SearchPathFrom` climbs from the fixture dir to `/`, merging host files from every ancestor of `TMPDIR` (the real home when TMPDIR lives under it) plus `/etc/mcpx/config.json`.\n\nFix, mirroring #7686: seed `MCPX_PATHS_CONFIG` with exactly the fixture file (no null — the seed replaces the walk outright) and clear the in-process flag seed, so the merged load merges the fixture anywhere TMPDIR lives and whatever the host exports. The leak paths are named in the test comment and the commit message.\n\nVerified on the laptop:\n\n- Reproduced the filed failure on the unfixed test by exporting an ambient seed: `config_test.go:216: a merged load lost the ignored key: []` — FAIL; with the fix under the same ambient seed — PASS.\n- `go test ./internal/config/ -count=1` — full package PASS.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1797502234&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=11207&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F11207&signature=2da657b8ace97311c0f9004bd1705c8e1ffe0fe19cd06466272292e7300c439f\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.