      "body": "Implements the still-missing run-seed transport from #1949 (Approach C), reusing the landed `gen` derivation (#1956) and seedstore/collector (#1953). Queue task 13250.\n\n## What lands\n\n- **`internal/testsupport/seed`** — the lazy helper. `MCPX_TEST_SEED` is read only when a test asks for a stream (`seed.Source(t, \"name\", version)`), so unrelated packages stay cacheable; there is no TestMain anywhere. Set + valid → used as-is (any `[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,128}` id replays; only wrapper/CI mint, and they mint UUIDv7). Unset in CI → fail closed. Unset locally → mint once per process with a warning. On failure the helper logs the exact one-command replay. The package doc is the #172 test-only env allowlist entry (same shape as `MCPX_TEST_REQUIRE`'s).\n- **`pkgs/mcpx/scripts/test.sh`** — the wrapper entrypoint: mints once if unset (warns, records to gitignored `.cache/test-seed/`), validates, exports the seed to every `go test` process, derives `-shuffle` from the same seed, fails closed in CI. Root `.gitignore` gains a negation so the script is tracked despite the `test.*` rule.\n- **`mcpx.yml`** — new `seed` job mints one UUIDv7 per run (or accepts the new `workflow_dispatch` `seed` input for exact replay), uploads `seed.json` as the `test-seed` artifact the #1953 collector files into `testdata/seeds/v1`, and `test` / `stress-pr` / `stress-nightly` now `need` it and receive `MCPX_TEST_SEED`. The stress jobs derive `-shuffle` from the run seed instead of `RUN_IDENTITY`; re-running failed jobs reuses the seed because the successful seed job is not re-run.\n- **`mcpx-test.yml`** — `init` mints and outputs the seed; `unit` and `e2e` jobs receive it; the wrapper regression tests run in the unit job.\n- **`TESTING.md`** — run-seed section: wrapper usage, the bare-`go test` per-package limitation, CI behaviour, replay.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `go test ./internal/testsupport/seed/ ./internal/seedstore/ -count=1` — pass (laptop). `go vet` clean, `gofmt` clean, `bash -n` clean.\n- Wrapper unittest (`scripts/tests/test_mcpx_test_seed.py`, fake-`go` oracle: asserts the exact argv + env the test process receives) — 4 tests pass.\n- The shuffle derivation is implemented three times (Go helper, wrapper, workflow python) and cross-checked: seed `01a0f101-2378-7c1c-9dc1-5a1ae1571eca` → `6825000031865948415` in all three. The Go test restates the formula from #1949 section 2 with raw sha256 as its oracle, and pins `Mint` against `seedstore.Timestamp` (the store's independent UUIDv7 parser).\n- Both workflow files parse as YAML; job graph checked (`seed` has no needs; `budget`'s existing needs are unaffected).\n\n## Pre-existing failure (not a regression)\n\n`internal/testsupport/gen` `TestConfigLayersProperty` fails identically on a clean worktree at origin/main `6f1efc4424` — the merged-servers map leaks the host machine's real mcpx config into the fixture expectation. Filed as #7686.\n\nScope guards honoured: PR #5127 untouched; the landed derivation/store work is reused, not redone.\n\nCloses the transport remainder of #1949.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796734147&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7690&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7690&signature=37fd71bc9baf42280be6f43f0166aa86e920a81054d8620025fad3663d95ab05\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7690?aut